<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The platform's own pages. Hand-maintained, and short on purpose: these are the only URLs that
  exist without a database behind them.

  Storefronts (/s/<slug>) are deliberately ABSENT. There is one per merchant, they appear and are
  suspended without a deploy, and this file is a static asset baked at build time — so any list of
  them here would be stale the first time a shop signs up. Listing them needs a generator that
  reads the active shops at build (or a served /sitemap.xml), which is a separate change with its
  own failure mode: a build that cannot reach the database must not silently ship an empty sitemap.
  Until then they are reachable and crawlable, just not enumerated here — robots.txt allows /s/.

  Absolute URLs are required by the sitemap protocol, so the production host is hardcoded. It must
  match the host in the og:image tags in index.html.
-->
